(6184188, 911145, 30982, '<td valign="top">I was about to say what Johanna said (tanguera) - blemishes quite often to me are features.  They add life.  This is wonderfully titled, too - the blues make this rich and vibrant, and the bokeh is lovely!  Congrats on your new #1, too (though I still quite like your #2 shot, too!)</td>', 'I was about to say what Johanna said (tanguera) - blemishes quite often to me are features.  They add life.  This is wonderfully titled, too - the blues make this rich and vibrant, and the bokeh is lovely!  Congrats on your new #1, too (though I still quite like your #2 shot, too!)', '2010-10-07 02:52:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(6184226, 911365, 30364, '<td valign="top">Another <i>great</i> brown!  I could not bring myself to vote on Negative Image, nor even to look.  But now that I have done so, I have obviously started at the right end!  Brilliant suspension of all that''s tedious about photography, in favor of all that''s bewitching.  Thank you Brian.  I can see I must pull my socks up (down) if I am to keep up with you down here in the DPC dirt.<br/> <br/>ETA:  I think I may have your measure in Monuments and Memorials however.  Stand by.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2010-10-07 03:27:14.</i></td>', 'Another great brown!  I could not bring myself to vote on Negative Image, nor even to look.  But now that I have done so, I have obviously started at the right end!  Brilliant suspension of all that''s tedious about photography, in favor of all that''s bewitching.  Thank you Brian.  I can see I must pull my socks up (down) if I am to keep up with you down here in the DPC dirt. ETA:  I think I may have your measure in Monuments and Memorials however.  Stand by.', '2010-10-07 04:25:28.000000', '2010-10-07 04:27:14.000000', 0),
(6184468, 910877, 113419, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>These shots always draw a WOW from me I first see them.  Yours, as a negative image is even more so.  I''m a "does the title work" type gal so that was the next thing and I loved it....the title and the modern day gps just clicked with me.  What I got out of the complete picture was, "Our societies today are so fast pace, we really need to slow down."  <br/>From reading your notes I don''t think you were trying to drive home any "lessons" with this shot but it did for me.<br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>First of all, I don''t understand the composition cause you are on the wrong side of your car! - just kidding ;-)  The composition is really good.  Someone mentioned that the rearview blocked their view but I don''t see it as a problem.  For me it looks exactly as it should.  The somewhat tilted dash agains the curvy road just works!  The negative color works well in this photo.<br/> <br/> <br/>Challenge:<br/>You were right on target with this. <br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>Very well done artistically.  And emotionally, well as explained above in "First Impressions" it did speak to me on an emotional level.  I feel that for the most part we "drive" ourselves too hard in our day to day lives and your shot just underscored that for me.<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>I believe you did a good job with this.  You were looking for a mid-5 in your score so I''d say that you accomplished your goal.  And you had a good overall effect.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  First Impressions: These shots always draw a WOW from me I first see them.  Yours, as a negative image is even more so.  I''m a "does the title work" type gal so that was the next thing and I loved it....the title and the modern day gps just clicked with me.  What I got out of the complete picture was, "Our societies today are so fast pace, we really need to slow down."  From reading your notes I don''t think you were trying to drive home any "lessons" with this shot but it did for me. Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): First of all, I don''t understand the composition cause you are on the wrong side of your car! - just kidding ;-)  The composition is really good.  Someone mentioned that the rearview blocked their view but I don''t see it as a problem.  For me it looks exactly as it should.  The somewhat tilted dash agains the curvy road just works!  The negative color works well in this photo.  Challenge:You were right on target with this.  Artistic/Emotion: Very well done artistically.  And emotionally, well as explained above in "First Impressions" it did speak to me on an emotional level.  I feel that for the most part we "drive" ourselves too hard in our day to day lives and your shot just underscored that for me. Summary: I believe you did a good job with this.  You were looking for a mid-5 in your score so I''d say that you accomplished your goal.  And you had a good overall effect. ', '2010-10-07 10:35:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(6184534, 911463, 106233, '<td valign="top">Great picture!<br/>Fantastic idea and execution. New fave.<br/>Congratulations!</td>', 'Great picture!Fantastic idea and execution. New fave.Congratulations!', '2010-10-07 11:13:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(6184615, 911419, 113419, '<td valign="top"><br/><b>Greetings from the Critique Club</b> <br/> <br/>First Impressions: <br/>My first impression was, "Oh What Fun!"  I really enjoyed this picture.  <br/> <br/>Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): <br/>Someone mentioned in the comments that they didn''t like the cropping of the wheel; but I really don''t think it takes   away from the image.  Having just the tops of the tents and booths only added to the overall composure.  In fact, for me, it shows how ferris wheels and carnivals/fairs are actually larger than life!  I mean, think of the excitment that is generated when the fair comes to town.  It''s something that can''t be contained!<br/> <br/>Challenge: <br/>Bingo!  You hit the nail on the head.<br/> <br/>Artistic/Emotion: <br/>A very good artistic shot!  I see you placed in abstract and digital art....what a good home for this image.<br/>I just don''t see how any one good look at this and not get a happy feel from it.  It made me smile.<br/> <br/>Summary: <br/>I don''t understand why this shot didn''t finish any better than it did.  It totally did it for me.  I like the spots of color against the white and the blues are wonderful.  I really don''t have any suggestions for making this better because I think it''s a GREAT image just as it is.<br/> <br/>Looking forward to seeing more of your work.  :-)</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club  First Impressions: My first impression was, "Oh What Fun!"  I really enjoyed this picture.   Technical (Comp, lighting, color, focus): Someone mentioned in the comments that they didn''t like the cropping of the wheel; but I really don''t think it takes   away from the image.  Having just the tops of the tents and booths only added to the overall composure.  In fact, for me, it shows how ferris wheels and carnivals/fairs are actually larger than life!  I mean, think of the excitment that is generated when the fair comes to town.  It''s something that can''t be contained! Challenge: Bingo!  You hit the nail on the head. Artistic/Emotion: A very good artistic shot!  I see you placed in abstract and digital art....what a good home for this image.I just don''t see how any one good look at this and not get a happy feel from it.  It made me smile. Summary: I don''t understand why this shot didn''t finish any better than it did.  It totally did it for me.  I like the spots of color against the white and the blues are wonderful.  I really don''t have any suggestions for making this better because I think it''s a GREAT image just as it is. Looking forward to seeing more of your work.  :-)', '2010-10-07 12:55:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(6184627, 911717, 59267, '<td valign="top">The gravity looks mysterious which is a good wow factor. Congratulations on your ribbon!</td>', 'The gravity looks mysterious which is a good wow factor. Congratulations on your ribbon!', '2010-10-07 13:12:25.000000', NULL, 0);
